content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-102 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-19870, filtered-water line; this line is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal leakage: the reported steady drip of approximately one drop per second matches the manual symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal'. The manual's corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check. No numerical allowable leakage rate or leak-rate limit is provided in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. The reported drive-end value of 2.1 mm/s is below the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/Zone B boundary and, if confirmed as an RMS velocity reading, falls in Zone A (0.0–2.8, 'New machines'). It is not in Zone D (7.1–11.0), so the highest-severity-zone immediate-stop and reliability-engineer notification rule is not triggered by this reading. Only the drive-end reading is available; the manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: the applicable bearing-housing surface limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reported 66 C drive-end housing temperature is 4 C below the normal upper limit, 14 C below alarm and 24 C below trip. It therefore does not indicate high bearing temperature and does not meet SSP-07's requirement for a priority-1 work order within the shift, which applies only above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall disposition: the available vibration and temperature readings do not require an immediate stop, but the active shaft-seal leak requires planned seal replacement rather than continued acceptance without repair. P2 is a planning recommendation for this work; SSP-07 supplies no general P2/P3 response-time criteria for seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces — most directly consistent with the steady shaft-seal leakage; confirm the seal condition during disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Previous dry running or loss of seal flush — a listed cause of shaft-seal leakage. This pump has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry; flush status and any dry-running history remain unconfirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment — also listed as a possible cause of seal leakage. It is not confirmed by the report; perform the specified laser alignment check and record the result.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Apply the safety controls listed below. Electrically isolate and lock out at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge, drain and vent before the line break, and drain the pump for seal replacement. Remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly using the signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15",
        "C02",
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Withdraw the existing mechanical seal and shaft sleeve; inspect and record the seal-face condition and inspect the sleeve for scoring, including the scoring depth if any is found. Record any evidence of dry running or loss of flush.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Fit one new HF3-450 component mechanical seal and one new HF3-120 casing gasket. Do not substitute HF3-450B: the bulletin supersession does not apply to serial HF3-19870. Replace the HF3-455 sleeve only if its inspection establishes that replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Reassemble and tighten the disturbed fasteners to Table 5 with lightly oiled threads, as applicable: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm; and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. The gland torque for this pump is 25 Nm, not the bulletin value of 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "5. Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool after reassembly and whenever work has moved the motor or bearing housing. Documented tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "6. Before returning the pump to service, restore and verify the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge. Do not run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "7. At closeout, inspect and record the mechanical-seal leakage condition and any residual drip rate without assigning an unsupported numerical acceptance limit. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings in mm/s RMS, classify the highest reading using Figure 3, and record the bearing-housing temperature for comparison with the 70/80/90 C limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type — required replacement. Pumps below serial HF3-22000 continue to use this seal rather than HF3-450B.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket — fit new whenever the casing is opened and as required by the seal-replacement procedure.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve — conditional spare only, not an automatic replacement; have one available if inspection finds scoring requiring sleeve replacement. The documented 0.1 mm scoring threshold in SB-2026-014 does not apply to this serial.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Because this task is inside the pump and on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding SSP-07's 25 kg lifting threshold. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-102 is within the P-101 to P-106 filtered-water pump group dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for the work.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current 2.1 mm/s reading is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone and 66 C is below the alarm limit, so the SSP-07 immediate-stop/reliability-notification and priority-1 temperature controls are not presently triggered. If subsequent vibration measurements classify the highest reading as Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: standard labour allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician; included because seal-leakage troubleshooting calls for an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number and gland torque: Table 5 and the parts list specify HF3-450 with 25 Nm seal-gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, specifies HF3-450B and 30 Nm. The bulletin applies only to serial HF3-22000 and above. P-102 is HF3-19870, so the manual's HF3-450 seal and 25 Nm torque apply; the bulletin explicitly says pumps below HF3-22000 continue using HF3-450 and Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve scoring: the manual requires inspection for scoring but gives no numerical rejection depth. SB-2026-014's instruction to replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm is within the instructions for pumps built from serial HF3-22000; it is therefore not adopted as the documented limit for HF3-19870.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 2.1 mm/s vibration value an RMS velocity measurement, and what is the non-drive-end bearing-housing reading? Both housings must be measured and the highest reading classified under the manual method (C06, C07).",
    "What numerical mechanical-seal leakage limit, if any, and what post-repair leakage acceptance criterion apply to this pump? The evidence identifies leakage and its corrective action but gives no allowable drip rate (C09).",
    "What shaft-sleeve scoring rejection limit applies to pumps below serial HF3-22000? The manual requires inspection but supplies no depth limit, and the 0.1 mm bulletin criterion is not applicable to this serial (C10, C13).",
    "What are the as-found seal-face condition, sleeve condition, alignment values and seal-flush/dry-running history? These are needed to distinguish the listed probable causes and must be recorded during the work (C02, C09, C10).",
    "What required completion date or site P2/P3 response-time standard applies to an active seal leak? SSP-07 defines the priority-1 response for bearing temperature above alarm but provides no general seal-leak prioritisation or P2/P3 deadlines (C15)."
  ]
}
